# Cline rules -- streamslop digging game

## Boot order (read at session start, in this order)

1. `docs/instructions.md` -- the canonical rules file. It governs; what
   follows is only its operational summary.
2. `docs/ROADMAP.md` -- the working roadmap: milestones 0.0.1 through
   0.1.0, with scope, exit tests, and the feel checklist. The only doc
   describing future work in detail.
3. `docs/GDD.md` -- design law, final-form (current systems and
   ship-plan; no history). When behavior and design disagree, the design
   docs win and the code is wrong.
4. `docs/dev_log.md` -- the development log: session rulings, changelogs,
   supersessions. Evidence, not law; consult when provenance matters.
5. `docs/PROJECT_MAP.md` -- auto-generated map of every script and
   function, with docstrings. Generated by the comment auditor; never
   hand-edit it.

## The One Rule (spiritual)

`dig.gd` may be touched -- refactors, engine upgrades, bug fixes,
netcode seams. What may never change is the player-facing experience
(`docs/GDD.md` §2):

- One verb. The verb set is `{dig}` and it stays that size.
- Swing rate 0.45s. Never tuned, never upgraded, never buffed by
  anything.
- Depth is infinite. Width is purchasable. Never the reverse.
- Nothing ever happens in the hole.
- The clang.

Enforcement: corey's conscience (corey is the human, in GDD fiction). Not
CI. CI enforces exactly one real thing -- the credits.

## Laws on every session

- There are no tests. There will never be tests. The feel checklist
  (`docs/ROADMAP.md` §4) is the entire regression suite; a failed
  checkbox blocks the tag. CI enforces nothing about gameplay.
- Autoloads: DirtBus, GameState, Attribution -- in that order. DirtBus
  is the only bus. Signals may be appended, never removed. There will
  never be a second bus.
- Version stays 0.x. Bumps only at milestone gates.
- The Godot project lives in `godot/`; `res://` is `godot/`'s root.
  Repo-level docs and tooling (this file, `docs/`, `tools/`, `.github/`)
  live at the repo root, witchgame-style. Two roots, on purpose.
- GDScript: tabs, 4-wide. Comment house discipline as in witchgame
  (3-line `##` file header, one `##` docstring above every func, single
  `#` one-liners inside bodies) -- honored by hand; there is no linter
  here and there will never be one.

## Gates before you call any change done

1. `python3 tools/build_project_map.py` exits 0 -- comment house style
   conforms and `docs/PROJECT_MAP.md` is regenerated.
2. `python3 tools/attr_lint.py` exits 0 -- every asset file under
   `godot/assets/` is claimed in `godot/assets/catalog.json`.
3. After adding or moving any script with `class_name`, rescan first
   (task "streamslop: Godot class rescan (headless)") or reload the
   project in the open editor -- otherwise headless runs lie.
4. When a milestone closes: the feel checklist, by hand, in full.

## Working agreements

- Small, scoped diffs; one concern per change. Nothing is committed and
  nothing is pushed without an explicit human go.
- Design ambiguities: ask, never assume (`docs/GDD.md` is the canonical
  vision, updateable by the human at any time).
- Memory bank duty: update `docs/` at the end of every working session,
  whenever the human reports a milestone or ruling, and whenever the
  bank has drifted from reality.
